  "body": "Stacked on #1070 (on #1060). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n- `Tool` gains `cutting: Vec<CuttingRow>` (new `camcraft_tools::cutting_rows`). Each row is `{material, rpm, feed}`, keyed by the built-in `WorkMaterial` groups the document's material already uses. The tool's own `rpm`/`feed` stay the running numbers the post reads, and the fallback.\n- Seeding happens only through commands, one undo step each:\n  - `SetWorkMaterial` re-seeds every tool that has a row for the new material (`ChangeTool`), plus the milling feed of each op on such a tool (`EditOperationParams`). The status line says how many moved.\n  - `AddTool` starts on the document material's row.\n  - A `ChangeTool` that edits only the table loads the row. An Apply that also states rpm/feed keeps its own numbers.\n  - `EditOperationLinks` (tool retarget) takes the new tool's row feed.\n  - Quick-add, MCP `add_operation` and the recognizer seed a new op's feed. An explicit MCP params patch still wins.\n- **Nothing moves on load.** With no matching row, everything stays as it is today.\n- File: an additive `cutting_data` key on `ToolDto`, written only when the tool has rows. A tool without rows saves byte-identical, so there is no version step. An unknown material word refuses the file by name.\n- Validation by tool name at `AddTool`/`ChangeTool` (and `is_sane` at read): rpm and feed must be finite and above zero (a torch row states rpm 0), and no material may appear twice.\n- Tool editor: a new collapsed \"Cutting data by material\" header (`tool_cutting_rows.rs`) with per-row material, rpm, feed, Remove, and \"Add material row\". The Body column is untouched (#1043).\n- MCP: `add_tool`'s `definition` takes `cutting_data`, and `get_job` shows it. Stating the material over MCP is still #732; editing a tool is #1062.\n- Decisions are in `docs/decisions/890-cutting-data-per-material.md`, including the #1060 interaction: Update/Replace still match by name and import rows and running numbers as the library states them, with no re-seed.\n\n## How tested\nPinning tests, all in `crates/app/tests/tool_cutting_rows.rs`:\n- `a_tool_without_rows_writes_no_key_and_a_table_round_trips`\n- `a_project_without_rows_saves_byte_identical_and_a_table_survives_save_load`\n- `loading_never_moves_the_numbers_an_existing_project_runs`\n- `an_unknown_material_word_refuses_the_file_by_name`\n- `the_table_round_trips_the_tool_library`\n- `unusable_rows_are_refused_by_tool_name_at_creation`\n- `stating_the_material_seeds_tool_and_ops_in_one_undo_step`\n- `an_op_on_material_x_posts_x_rows_spindle_speed` (posts S3100/F410 for the steel row)\n- `adding_a_tool_and_editing_its_table_seed_the_running_numbers`\n- `quick_add_and_retarget_seed_the_op_feed_from_the_row`\n- `mcp_add_tool_takes_the_table_and_refuses_a_bad_row`\n\nAlso unit tests `cutting_rows::tests` (tools) and `tool_cutting_rows::tests::rows_add_per_material_and_ride_the_draft_both_ways` (ui).\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/898-tool-catalog-fields` green on the final head 78a23c8b (tools, motion, app, ui suites - 4 steps, 0 failed, 3.3 min); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nNo golden moved: no fixture tool has rows, and the posted numbers still come from `Tool::rpm` and the op feed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The editor widget was not clicked by hand; only the draft round-trip is unit-tested. No structural/snapshot assertion was added, because the header is collapsed by default for a tool without rows.\n- With a dirty op-page draft, a retarget's seeded feed can be overwritten by a later Apply of that draft. That is the draft's normal last-write-wins behaviour.\n- MCP `add_operation` seeding is not driven end to end, because MCP cannot state the material yet (#732). The seed fn it calls is pinned directly.\n\nChangelog: A tool can carry cutting data (rpm, feed) per workpiece material; stating the material, adding the tool or editing its table loads the matching row into the tool and its operations' feed, one undo step; old files load and save unchanged (#890)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #890\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
